WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.569
-No matter who the Mayor
of New York is, we hate him,

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.270
and then, by the time he goes,
we're like,

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.106
"That's the mayor.
We love him," you know.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:08.774
Like Bloomberg, we hated.
He'd be on --

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:11.110
He'd come out and like cover
the city in beige carpeting,

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.412
and then, be like,
"Shoes off."

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.147
And we'd be like, "Ah!"

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.049
And then, by the time he left,
we were like,

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.416
"Hey, it's Mayor Bloomberg."

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:19.919
And now we hate him again.
It's a cycle.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:24.457 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:25.825 line:0%
-Congrats on everything,
I got to say.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:26.959 line:0%
-Thank you, man.
Thanks so much for having me.

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:29.262 line:0%
-I'm so excited.
I'm looking forward to the show.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.796 line:0%
Now, I know you -- I know
your stand-up pretty well.

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:32.131 line:0%
When did you start
doing stand-up?

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:34.467 line:0%
-I started doing stand-up
when I was about 19 years old,

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.035
and I started in New York
but then

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.571
I went on the road right away
just 'cause those actually pay.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.473
'Cause shows in New York's
like nine people,

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.642
and eight of them are comics.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.143
And one of them's, like,
a pile of clothes,

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:47.080
so I went on the road
to do shows right away.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.316
Like, I was doing --
I remember in my early 20s,

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:53.653
I was doing a show
in Murfreesboro, Tennessee.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.455
Murfreesboro.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.922
I'm pronouncing it correctly.
-Okay, okay.

00:00:56.922 --> 00:00:58.524
-I'm not mispronouncing it.
-You're not -- no.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:00.426
-That's how it's pronounced.
-That's a place.

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:01.894
-Murfreesboro.

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:05.264
It was -- I think it was named
by a dying Confederate general

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:08.000
as he barely sat up in bed
eating mashed potatoes,

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.435
and his grandson was like,

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:10.803
"Pappy,
you got to name the town!"

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:12.438
And he was like,
[Slurring] "Murfreesboro."

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:13.573
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:16.109
They're like,
"Put it on the sign!"

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.576
[ Applause ]

00:01:17.576 --> 00:01:19.612
-It is an odd name.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.114
-There's about nine R's
in "Murfreesboro."

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:23.283
But I was doing stand-up.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.784
This is one of the worst shows
I ever had.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:27.954
I was doing stand-up comedy in
Murfreesboro, Tennessee,

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:30.389
at an outdoor campground
next to a beer truck.

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:31.491
-Oh!

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:32.958
This sounds awful.

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:34.461
-Well, later, some would allege

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:36.262
that I was blocking
the beer truck.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.296
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:38.832
And I disagree with them.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:40.633
-I was doing the show
on purpose --

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.101
I was doing the show on purpose.
-Of course you were.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:43.169
-And it sounds awful,
but it wasn't a mistake.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.503
-It was a gig.

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:46.705
-Yeah, it wasn't like
I was driving across the south

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:48.274
in an old jalopy
and it broke down,

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.042
and the people in Murfreesboro
were like,

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:51.311
"We'll give you supper,

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.245
but you got to make funnies
for us tonight." Like...

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:56.148
I meant to do it.
I had it on my calendar.

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:57.650
I was like, "Oh, boy, oh, boy,

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.253
only two more weeks until the
worst night in my entire life."

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.254
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.089
-But they didn't appreciate you?

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.258
-Well, no! I got to the show.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.527
And I put "show" in many quotes.

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:08.527
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:09.929
-How many quotes?

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:13.399
-Just as many quotes as there
are R's in "Murfreesboro."

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.433
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:16.669
Take all the R's
and make them quotes.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:19.672
I get out on the stage,
and the stage was really nice.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.108
It was a lot like this,
except not at all.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.843
It was a couple 2x4s
lying in dirt.

00:02:24.843 --> 00:02:27.947
I start to perform
stand-up comedy, okay?

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.615
And one guy yelled from the back

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:31.617
what is the best heckle
I've heard in my life.

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:33.952
He yelled, [Southern accent]
"Excuse me, sir.

00:02:33.952 --> 00:02:35.788
I think
I speak for everyone here

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.790
when I say
that we would enjoy silence

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.159
more than
the sound of your voice."

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:41.827
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:43.963
-What?!
-Yes.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.032
Insanely mean, no?

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.968
But also, how very eloquent.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.136
-That is
the most eloquent heckle

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:51.136
I've ever heard in my life.

00:02:51.136 --> 00:02:52.504
-It's a beautiful
turn of phrase,

00:02:52.504 --> 00:02:54.506
to enjoy silence more
than the sound of your voice.

00:02:54.506 --> 00:02:57.477
If that was, like, the last line
of a Maya Angelou poem,

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.746
you would just shut the book
and look out the window.

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.280
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.949 line:0%
-Here you are -- you're hosting
"Saturday Night Live" this week

00:03:03.949 --> 00:03:04.951 line:0%
for the second time.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.252 line:0%
-Second time, which is great.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.454 line:0%
I was nervous. Some people
don't get to come back.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:09.655 line:0%
-That's true.

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:11.257 line:0%
They do controversial things,
like they tear up

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.359 line:0%
a picture of the pope
or they are Robert Blake.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.094 line:0%
And they don't get to --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.529
They don't get to be
on the show again.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.930
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.199
-"They are Robert Blake."

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:21.133
-They are Robert Blake,
the person.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.302
-No, exactly.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.370
But I mean, you should be
kind of used to it.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.972
You were a writer on
"Saturday Night Live" in 2009,

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:28.307
I want to say.

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:31.009
-Yeah, from like '08 to 2012,
I was a writer there.

00:03:31.009 --> 00:03:33.612
And -- well, it's totally
different, though, now,

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:35.448
because I'm on camera,

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.784
whereas before,
I was like a busboy and now,

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.819
I'm the maitre D.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.787
-Yeah, but did you ever think
that you would host?

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.923
-No, I mean, I auditioned to be
on the show,

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.257
but I was hired as a writer,

00:03:45.257 --> 00:03:47.794
because I was auditioning
and I remember they went "No."

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.027
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.027 --> 00:03:51.230
But then, I would get on camera
occasionally.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.365
But the idea of hosting
is totally surreal.

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:54.634
-Well, it's a great cast.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.835
I mean, you're gonna be --
you're in good hands.

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:58.304
-It's really been the most fun.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:01.073
-Do you remember the first time
you were ever in a sketch, ever?

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:03.776
-Yeah, I was in -- it wasn't on
"Update" or anything.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:06.245
I was just like
a clipboard operator, you know,

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:07.279
when they go like, "Take five."

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:09.048
-I've done that.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:13.285
I was in an Activia yogurt
commercial sketch

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:15.088
with Kristen Wiig
and Jason Sudeikis.

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:16.422
-Oh, and she was
Jamie Lee Curtis.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:17.857
-She was Jamie Lee Curtis.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:21.927
And Activia yogurt allegedly
gave you diarrhea at the time.

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:23.329
I think was the premise.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.430
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.432
And I come in,
I go, like, "Take one."

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:29.435
And I snapped it, then I walked
off camera, you know.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.103
They go, like,
"This way, this way."

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:32.938
And then Bobby Moynihan
was there,

00:04:32.938 --> 00:04:34.173
and it was my first time
on camera,

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:37.042
so we start high-fiving,
like a lot.

00:04:37.042 --> 00:04:38.778
Like way too much for one line.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:40.779
-Yeah, but he was so psyched
for you.

00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:43.349
-And then, I look over
and Lorne is staring at us.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:46.118
Like this, and I'm just
high-fiving him, and I see him.

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:48.954
And then, I realize that I'm
late and I've missed my cue.

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:52.291
And I ran back on and was like,
"Take five."

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:54.994
And, like, it was a full lull.

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.562
I thought no one caught it.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:59.965
I get to the after party, and
our mutual friend Neal Brennan

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:02.568
comes over to me and he goes,
"Hey, man, great job.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.437
You were five seconds late
on that second cue."

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:05.437
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.437 --> 00:05:06.605
-Yeah, people can see it,
I mean --

00:05:06.605 --> 00:05:07.807
-Oh, it was -- yeah.

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:09.409
-But I mean, I don't know
if you guys remember,

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:10.909
but we actually have a clip.

00:05:10.909 --> 00:05:12.245
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:14.914
Here's John Mulaney
missing his cue

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:17.083
in his first-ever
"Saturday Night Live" sketch.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:18.317
Check it.

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:20.086
-I killed this Activia.
Can I get another one?

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.587
-Yeah, of course, yeah.
Here you go.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:22.855
Here you go.
-Thank you.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.624 line:0%
-I'll take one for myself.
I'll keep going here.

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:28.561 line:0%
All right,
let's do this. Here we go.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:31.464 line:0%
-Activia testimonial number two.

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.299 line:0%
-Oh, my God. You were a bit --

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:35.701
Neal Brennan
is almost exactly right.

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.004
-Yeah.
Wait, I was remarkably calm.

00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:39.104
-Yeah, you were.

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:40.439
-I was like,
"I don't know, take two."

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:41.773
I was high-fiving. I'm sorry.

00:05:41.773 --> 00:05:43.209
-You were just jumping up
and down with Bobby Moynihan.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:44.277
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:45.277
-You're gonna crush it
this weekend.

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:46.379
We love you, buddy.

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:47.613
-Thank you, buddy.
Thank you for having me.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.715
-Please, John Mulaney,
everybody.

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:51.550 line:0%
-There was a thing saying
you might run for mayor.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.986 line:0%
-For New York.
No, New York, not South Bend.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:55.788 line:0%
-No, for mayor of New York City?
-Yeah, I know,

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:58.291 line:0%
I'm going to
start with New York.

00:05:58.291 --> 00:05:59.492 line:0%
Listen, no.

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:02.195
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:05.564
It's not --
Thank you, I appreciate that.

00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:09.902
-Standing ovation.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:12.271
Thank you.
[ Cheering continues ]

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:13.673
-Please.
-They were ready for it.

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:14.941
It's unbelievable.

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:17.442
-Thank you.
Please, sit down.

00:06:17.442 --> 00:06:18.911
Please sit down.
-Here he is.

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:21.080
-Please sit.
-John Mulaney!

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.082
-Please.
-Mayor Mulaney!

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:25.918
-Earlier this evening,
I called Mayor de Blasio

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:28.921
and I conceded because I got
zero votes, and --

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.256
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:33.259
No, I don't know why I got this
in my head.

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:34.627
I know why.
I had, like, too much --

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.295
I had like a month
where I wasn't doing anything.

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:37.596
-Yeah.
-So...

00:06:37.596 --> 00:06:38.898
I was walking around New York.

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.332
I was getting so angry about
things.

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:42.802
You know, there was --
so I said --

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:44.403
I came home and I said,
"I'm going to run for mayor,"

00:06:44.403 --> 00:06:46.071
to my wife, you know?
-Yeah.

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:49.274
-And she said, "Okay, but you
have to think about stuff

00:06:49.274 --> 00:06:50.376
for all five boroughs.

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:51.777
It can't just be
things on our block."

00:06:51.777 --> 00:06:53.278
And I was like, "All right."

00:06:53.278 --> 00:06:55.781
But then, I just -- look.

00:06:55.781 --> 00:06:58.618
No matter who the Mayor
of New York is, we hate him,

00:06:58.618 --> 00:07:00.353
and then, by the time he goes,
we're like,

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:02.355
"That's the mayor.
We love him," you know.

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:04.890
Like Bloomberg, we hated.
He'd be on --

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:07.226
He'd come out and like cover
the city in beige carpeting,

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:08.594
and then, be like, "Shoes off."

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:10.396
And we'd be like, "Ah!"

00:07:10.396 --> 00:07:12.298
And then, by the time he left,
we were like,

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:13.599
"Hey, it's Mayor Bloomberg."

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.901
And now we hate him again.
It's a cycle.

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:17.636
-Yeah.
-So de Blasio is low, right?

00:07:17.636 --> 00:07:19.037
-Yeah.
-Remember --

00:07:19.037 --> 00:07:21.107
Were you at the Paul Simon
concert when de Blasio got up?

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.407
-Yeah, we were there together.
-Yeah.

00:07:22.407 --> 00:07:23.809
Remember, they're like,
"Ladies and gentlemen,

00:07:23.809 --> 00:07:25.377
Mayor de Blasio."

00:07:25.377 --> 00:07:27.412
"Boo!"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.412 --> 00:07:30.582
-It was louder than like
an encore for like "Graceland."

00:07:30.582 --> 00:07:32.217
-Yeah.
-They're like, "Whoo!"

00:07:32.217 --> 00:07:34.387
-It was like Vince McMahon
level theater.

00:07:34.387 --> 00:07:36.288
Like, "Boo!"

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:37.723
-Yeah, that was crazy.

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:40.059
-De Blasio walks out with his
stupid sideburns and --

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:42.795
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:45.764
But -- But I -- here's --
Okay. Here's --

00:07:45.764 --> 00:07:48.734
Look, I know I won't be good
as mayor.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:52.104
Okay? I know that.
But here's my thing.

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:54.139
I'm going to get rid
of Uber and Lyft,

00:07:54.139 --> 00:07:55.975
and if you don't like it,

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:57.977
you can get rid of me
in two years.

00:07:57.977 --> 00:07:59.578
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.578 --> 00:08:01.847
But you can't --
There's a bus lane,

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:03.081
and then there's a bike lane,

00:08:03.081 --> 00:08:05.083
and then there's
one million new Ubers,

00:08:05.083 --> 00:08:06.752
and then there's
10 billion new Lyfts.

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:08.554
-Yeah.
-And it's just you can't do it.

00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:10.990
And I have a whole commercial
laid out.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.190
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:13.559
I mean, I haven't shot it,
but you know,

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:14.660
you can imagine it.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.762
You can imagine it.
I'm imagining it.

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:18.397
So here's the commercial.
All right.

00:08:18.397 --> 00:08:21.200
It's not fun, but it's --
this is just a good idea.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.934 --> 00:08:26.239
So it's an ambulance --
Shh, this is serious.

00:08:26.239 --> 00:08:28.074
So it's an ambulance,
and it's going

00:08:28.074 --> 00:08:29.908
up Sixth Avenue at 3:00 P.M.

00:08:29.908 --> 00:08:31.910
It's an ambulance.
Sirens are going, you know?

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:34.246
You feel the tension, right?
-What time of the day?

00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:36.215
-3:00 P.M.
-Yeah.

00:08:36.215 --> 00:08:38.650
It goes, it's 3:00 P.M.

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:43.089
It's not rush hour.
It's not lunchtime.

00:08:43.089 --> 00:08:44.923
And the streets are jammed.

00:08:44.923 --> 00:08:46.792
And then I'll have an actor
that looks like de Blasio

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:49.194
ride by on a bicycle, right?
[ Laughter ]

00:08:49.194 --> 00:08:50.529
And then it'll say,

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:52.597
"Now imagine someone you love
is in this ambulance."

00:08:52.597 --> 00:08:53.966
And then it goes, "boom."

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:56.101
And it says, "Bill de Blasio
said he'd fix everything

00:08:56.101 --> 00:08:57.636
in New York," which he didn't.
He didn't say that.

00:08:57.636 --> 00:08:59.438
But...
[ Laughter ]

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:00.873
-You can't put words
in his mouth.

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:02.408
-Oh, you can do that.
-You can't do that.

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:04.042
-I'm not going to put "quotes."
I'll say --

00:09:04.042 --> 00:09:05.577
I'll say he said something
like -- okay.

00:09:05.577 --> 00:09:06.746
Bill de Blasio was like,

00:09:06.746 --> 00:09:08.214
"I'm going to
fix everything in New York,"

00:09:08.214 --> 00:09:09.881
right?
-You're safe.

00:09:09.881 --> 00:09:11.383
-I'm in safe territory.
-My lawyer says you're safe.

00:09:11.383 --> 00:09:12.551
My lawyer says you're safe,
yeah.

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:14.720
-Good, yeah.
And then it will just say,

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.223
"John Mulaney as Mayor."
-Wow, that's pretty good.

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:19.391
-I think when you say -- yeah.
-That's a good, that's a...

00:09:19.391 --> 00:09:22.261
[ Cheers and applause ]
...memorable commercial.

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:24.263
And it hits a nerve.

00:09:24.263 --> 00:09:26.398
-I think it's, like,
mean-spirited.

00:09:26.398 --> 00:09:28.534
I don't like that I thought of
it, but once I thought of it,

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:31.437
I thought, like,
"That's a good idea."

00:09:31.437 --> 00:09:34.773
I -- I like Mayor de Blasio.

00:09:34.773 --> 00:09:38.911
I have had run-ins with him
that I found awkward.

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:42.247
I was hosting that Museum
of Natural History benefit

00:09:42.247 --> 00:09:43.716
that Mr. Lorne Michaels does.

00:09:43.716 --> 00:09:45.284
-Our boss.
-Yeah.

00:09:45.284 --> 00:09:47.052
The producer of
"Saturday Night Live."

00:09:47.052 --> 00:09:48.387
-And "The Tonight Show"
as well.

00:09:48.387 --> 00:09:49.588
-And "The Tonight Show," yeah,
-That's right.

00:09:49.588 --> 00:09:51.457
He's our producer.

00:09:51.457 --> 00:09:53.091
He produces everything
in this building.

00:09:53.091 --> 00:09:54.893
-Yeah, that's right, yeah.

00:09:54.893 --> 00:09:56.595
He's a good TV producer.

00:09:56.595 --> 00:09:59.231
-He's fantastic.
-Yeah, he's got hits.

00:09:59.231 --> 00:10:03.602
So he has this benefit
at the Natural History museum.

00:10:03.602 --> 00:10:06.238
Have you ever hosted it,
where you kind of go,

00:10:06.238 --> 00:10:07.739
"Welcome, everybody."
-Of course.

00:10:07.739 --> 00:10:09.241
-"This is --
Look at all the animals."

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:11.610
Because it's like the zoo,
but they're dead, you know.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:12.811
[ Laughter ]
-It's a museum.

00:10:12.811 --> 00:10:13.946
Yeah, it's a museum.

00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:15.681
-It's a museum
of animal bodies

00:10:15.681 --> 00:10:18.951
and what they would look like
next to fake trees and stuff.

00:10:18.951 --> 00:10:20.753
But it's a nice museum.
It's a great place.

00:10:20.753 --> 00:10:22.955
So I had --

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:24.790
I worked all day --
I worked for like three days

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:27.259
on all these jokes,
and most of them

00:10:27.259 --> 00:10:29.294
were de Blasio jokes.
-Yeah.

00:10:29.294 --> 00:10:33.132
-Because it's a New York
audience, and I, you know,

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:36.469
I mean, I opened --
I opened bad right away

00:10:36.469 --> 00:10:37.836
because I was like,
"This is great.

00:10:37.836 --> 00:10:40.806
I saw there's an elephant here.
So finally for one night,

00:10:40.806 --> 00:10:43.275
the elephant in the room for you
guys is not Jeffrey Epstein,"

00:10:43.275 --> 00:10:45.244
and -- yeah, right.
[ Audience ohs ]

00:10:45.244 --> 00:10:46.812
Just like you.

00:10:46.812 --> 00:10:50.649
Hey, no, but just like you,

00:10:50.649 --> 00:10:52.651
they were upset right away.
[ Applause ]

00:10:52.651 --> 00:10:55.855
-Yeah.
-And I said, but --

00:10:55.855 --> 00:10:57.990
[ Laughter ]

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.325
-It's a tough room.
-"But like Jeffrey Epstein,

00:10:59.325 --> 00:11:00.792
this elephant was murdered."

00:11:00.792 --> 00:11:02.728
I did a second part of the joke.
[ Audience ohs ]

00:11:02.728 --> 00:11:04.596
I know, right. Just --
Yeah, exactly.

00:11:04.596 --> 00:11:06.765
-But it's also --
But this is a good room.

00:11:06.765 --> 00:11:08.767
That room, I will say,
is a little tough.

00:11:08.767 --> 00:11:12.071
-You mean the museum with
the highest ceiling in the world

00:11:12.071 --> 00:11:13.638
and all the richest people
in the world

00:11:13.638 --> 00:11:14.907
