00:11:14.907 --> 00:11:16.942
It looks like an event the Joker
would crash into it.

00:11:16.942 --> 00:11:19.478
[ Laughter ]
And...

00:11:19.478 --> 00:11:21.113
-You should have opened
with that.

00:11:21.113 --> 00:11:22.448
You should have opened
with that one.

00:11:22.448 --> 00:11:24.150
You should have opened
with that.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:26.451
-Wait, I got to get
another chance.

00:11:26.451 --> 00:11:29.088
So then, I just did these
introductory remarks,

00:11:29.088 --> 00:11:31.823
two of which you just heard,
which were terrible jokes.

00:11:31.823 --> 00:11:35.327
So I sit down at the table,
and then, someone runs up

00:11:35.327 --> 00:11:38.797
and says, "Ladies and gentlemen,
we have a special guest here.

00:11:38.797 --> 00:11:41.633
Mayor Bill de Blasio has
dropped by the benefit."

00:11:41.633 --> 00:11:44.269
Now, this was called
a black tie event.

00:11:44.269 --> 00:11:46.638
Now that means that you wear
a tuxedo if you're a man.

00:11:46.638 --> 00:11:48.173
Now I'm not saying --
You're not a good per--

00:11:48.173 --> 00:11:50.175
I'm not saying you're a better
person if you're in a tuxedo,

00:11:50.175 --> 00:11:53.145
but Bill de Blasio walks up
in a light-blue suit

00:11:53.145 --> 00:11:56.515
with a bright-red tie,
like a clown.

00:11:56.515 --> 00:11:58.650
And...
[ Laughter ]

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.785
And they go, "Bill de Blasio."
And this is a nice event,

00:12:00.785 --> 00:12:02.253
and people go, "Boo!"

00:12:02.253 --> 00:12:04.256
And I hear one person go,
"Hiss!"

00:12:04.256 --> 00:12:05.624
-Wow.

00:12:05.624 --> 00:12:07.393
Wow. Bringing back the hiss.

00:12:07.393 --> 00:12:08.928
-So then, Mayor de Blasio
gets up.

00:12:08.928 --> 00:12:10.930
And no, he was not invited.

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:12.965
He had just left his
presidential campaign

00:12:12.965 --> 00:12:14.332
because he heard it was a lock

00:12:14.332 --> 00:12:16.234
and he didn't want the
pressure to get to him.

00:12:16.234 --> 00:12:19.071
So...
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.071 --> 00:12:21.773
He gets up, and he's like,
"Hi, it's me, the mayor."

00:12:21.773 --> 00:12:23.308
You know, he had to remind
everyone when he was mayor

00:12:23.308 --> 00:12:24.944
because he had run
for president.

00:12:24.944 --> 00:12:26.946
He's like, "I'm the mayor,
this is a great museum

00:12:26.946 --> 00:12:29.448
because they allow anyone
in here.

00:12:29.448 --> 00:12:32.250
Anyone of any
sexual orientation."

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.919
And everyone was like,
"Yeah, that's every museum.

00:12:33.919 --> 00:12:35.954
Like, there's..."
[ Laughter ]

00:12:35.954 --> 00:12:38.957
The only barrier to entry is
a suggested donation,

00:12:38.957 --> 00:12:40.426
which no one does.

00:12:40.426 --> 00:12:42.260
No one's keeping anyone
out of a museum.

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:44.963
-No.
-So then he said --

00:12:44.963 --> 00:12:48.800
So I, by the way, have
in my pocket a page of jokes

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.302
that are all about de Blasio.

00:12:50.302 --> 00:12:53.305
My next seven minutes was just
going to be de Blasio jokes.

00:12:53.305 --> 00:12:54.973
So then de Blasio says --
and it's all --

00:12:54.973 --> 00:12:57.977
"This event is run by
the great Lorne Michaels,

00:12:57.977 --> 00:12:59.445
an important person in New York,

00:12:59.445 --> 00:13:01.246
even though he's not
from New York."

00:13:01.246 --> 00:13:03.915
And I was like, "Oh, man."
[ Hissing ]

00:13:03.915 --> 00:13:06.252
Like, okay, yeah, right?
-Getting hisses right now.

00:13:06.252 --> 00:13:08.387
-Getting hissed.
-Someone's hissing over there.

00:13:08.387 --> 00:13:10.589
-So I get back --
So I turn to Lorne and I go,

00:13:10.589 --> 00:13:12.724
"I have a page
of de Blasio jokes."

00:13:12.724 --> 00:13:14.260
And Lorne goes, "Do them."

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:15.727
[ Laughter ]

00:13:15.727 --> 00:13:17.763 line:0%
♪♪

00:13:17.763 --> 00:13:19.063
-Dude.

00:13:19.063 --> 00:13:21.633
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:21.633 --> 00:13:24.436
-That New York thing --
that New York thing,

00:13:24.436 --> 00:13:26.305
like, when he said that,
I was like, "Oh!"

00:13:26.305 --> 00:13:28.607
And I know Lorne is from Canada.
I know it.

00:13:28.607 --> 00:13:31.076
And he talks about it. He'll go,
"I'm from Canada," you know?

00:13:31.076 --> 00:13:32.477
But if he looked me
in the eye and he went,

00:13:32.477 --> 00:13:33.745
"I'm from New York, right?"
I'd be like,

00:13:33.745 --> 00:13:34.980
"Yeah, yeah,
you're from New York."

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.281
-He's one of the most
New York people

00:13:36.281 --> 00:13:37.449
of all time.
-I know.

00:13:37.449 --> 00:13:38.783 line:0%
-Welcome back.
-Thank you, Jimmy.

00:13:38.783 --> 00:13:39.952 line:0%
-Thank you for being here.

00:13:39.952 --> 00:13:41.420 line:0%
Congrats on this movie,
by the way.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.255 line:0%
"Spider-Man:
Into the Spider-Verse."

00:13:43.255 --> 00:13:46.258 line:0%
I've never seen an animated film
like this ever in my lifetime.

00:13:46.258 --> 00:13:47.526 line:0%
It blew me away.

00:13:47.526 --> 00:13:49.794
-It's an absolutely
mind-blowing animated film.

00:13:49.794 --> 00:13:53.131
It, like, combines different
types of animation

00:13:53.131 --> 00:13:55.633
'cause it's bringing together
all these different universes

00:13:55.633 --> 00:13:59.504
of different spider-men, women,
and pigs in my case.

00:13:59.504 --> 00:14:03.575
-Now you play -- which I kind of
remember a little bit but --

00:14:03.575 --> 00:14:06.111
-Do you remember the character?
-I kind of a little bit, maybe.

00:14:06.111 --> 00:14:07.812
I don't know.
But there was a character.

00:14:07.812 --> 00:14:09.581
It was all
different types of spider-men,

00:14:09.581 --> 00:14:12.584
but you play Spider-Ham.

00:14:12.584 --> 00:14:13.718
[ Laughter ]

00:14:13.718 --> 00:14:16.588
Spider-Ham is Peter Porker.
-Yeah.

00:14:16.588 --> 00:14:17.756
[ Laughter ]

00:14:17.756 --> 00:14:20.759
-And was this, like,
a short-lived comic book?

00:14:20.759 --> 00:14:22.761
-Oh, no.
No, no, not short-lived.

00:14:22.761 --> 00:14:24.229
[ Laughter ]

00:14:24.229 --> 00:14:26.998
It was -- it was a spin-off
of sorts.

00:14:26.998 --> 00:14:28.767
I think started in 1983,

00:14:28.767 --> 00:14:31.637
and there are die-hard
Spider-Ham fans out there.

00:14:31.637 --> 00:14:34.039
-Honestly, this is
such a cool thing.

00:14:34.039 --> 00:14:35.440
I'm going in,

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:38.676
and I don't really know much
about comic books or Spider-Man.

00:14:38.676 --> 00:14:39.911
I know of them.

00:14:39.911 --> 00:14:42.147
-Well, I knew nothing about
the actual project

00:14:42.147 --> 00:14:43.815
when I first started recording.

00:14:43.815 --> 00:14:45.617
-About the project?
-Oh, yeah.

00:14:45.617 --> 00:14:48.787
So, I got a call,
and I said, "Hello." You know.

00:14:48.787 --> 00:14:49.855
[ Laughter ]

00:14:49.855 --> 00:14:52.024
-Good for you, though.
-Yeah.

00:14:52.024 --> 00:14:53.125
[ Laughter ]

00:14:53.125 --> 00:14:55.661
-Good improvising already.
-Absolutely.

00:14:55.661 --> 00:14:57.863
Nothing fancy, ordinary hello,
right?

00:14:57.863 --> 00:14:59.231
-No, great, hello, yeah.

00:14:59.231 --> 00:15:01.933
-And they said,
"This is a company, big company.

00:15:01.933 --> 00:15:03.569
Do you want to be in a movie?

00:15:03.569 --> 00:15:05.337
And we can't tell you
anything about it

00:15:05.337 --> 00:15:06.672
and we can't send you a script."

00:15:06.672 --> 00:15:08.306
Because when it's
these superhero things,

00:15:08.306 --> 00:15:09.741
they really keep them
under wraps.

00:15:09.741 --> 00:15:11.744
So, they said, "We can't tell
you anything about it.

00:15:11.744 --> 00:15:13.211
We can't send you a script."

00:15:13.211 --> 00:15:15.381
Which is how a lot of
kidnappings begin.

00:15:15.381 --> 00:15:16.782
[ Laughter ]

00:15:16.782 --> 00:15:20.018
But I was available, so...
[ Laughter ]

00:15:20.018 --> 00:15:22.020
-I'm up for an adventure.
Let's go for it.

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:24.556
-I was like, "All right.
Yeah, sure. What time? Where?"

00:15:24.556 --> 00:15:25.991
-Unmarked van.
-Yeah, okay.

00:15:25.991 --> 00:15:27.593
-Sure. Sounds cool.
[ Laughter ]

00:15:27.593 --> 00:15:29.694
-Cool. Blindfold? Fine.
[ Laughter ]

00:15:29.694 --> 00:15:35.601
So, I get to a building and,
you know, it's like Los Angeles.

00:15:35.601 --> 00:15:38.704
So it's not like a famous --
It's just a slab of concrete.

00:15:38.704 --> 00:15:41.273
And I go in, and Rodney Rothman
was there,

00:15:41.273 --> 00:15:43.608
