what's about to happen?"

00:15:43.608 --> 00:15:46.578
Which if it was a kidnapping is
a super creepy way to begin.

00:15:46.578 --> 00:15:48.347
[ Laughter ]
-That's even worse.

00:15:48.347 --> 00:15:49.782
"Do you know
what's about to happen?"

00:15:49.782 --> 00:15:51.717
-Yeah. These psychological games
are like, "Are you prepared?"

00:15:51.717 --> 00:15:52.817
[ Laughter ]

00:15:52.817 --> 00:15:54.320
-No.
-"For level two?"

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:56.688
So, they said,
"We're making this film."

00:15:56.688 --> 00:15:57.790
They explained it.

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:01.026
They said that the cast
was insane.

00:16:01.026 --> 00:16:02.360
-Oh, my gosh.

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:05.931
-Nicolas Cage, Hailee Steinfeld,
Mahershala Ali.

00:16:05.931 --> 00:16:08.033
-Mahershala Ali is unbelievable.

00:16:08.033 --> 00:16:09.401
-And Jake Johnson.

00:16:09.401 --> 00:16:11.070
I mean, it's, like,
a great group of people.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.338
I said,
"Who else are the actors in it?"

00:16:13.338 --> 00:16:14.739
And they said, "You."

00:16:14.739 --> 00:16:18.243
And I said, "I'm scared because
I've never been like --

00:16:18.243 --> 00:16:20.245
I've never not known
what a movie is

00:16:20.245 --> 00:16:22.281
and then I'm about to be
in the movie."

00:16:22.281 --> 00:16:24.716
-Yeah, and then be in a scene
with Nicolas Cage.

00:16:24.716 --> 00:16:27.753
-Yeah, and they said,
"Well, you play a superhero

00:16:27.753 --> 00:16:32.223
who is a pig who makes --"
[ Laughter ]

00:16:32.223 --> 00:16:35.094
"Who makes
nonstop outdated jokes."

00:16:35.094 --> 00:16:37.262
And I said, "I got it."
[ Laughter ]

00:16:37.262 --> 00:16:40.098
-"Yeah, I got this nailed."
-Absolutely nailed it.

00:16:40.098 --> 00:16:42.201
It's really fun, and, like,
I know this sounds like,

00:16:42.201 --> 00:16:43.601
I'm selling it,
but I kind of am, but --

00:16:43.601 --> 00:16:45.136
-Yeah, that's why you're here,
I guess.

00:16:45.136 --> 00:16:46.938
-Yeah, I guess that is why
we're really here in some way.

00:16:46.938 --> 00:16:48.007
-Yeah, me too. Yeah.

00:16:48.007 --> 00:16:51.409
-But it's like --
like, adults will like it

00:16:51.409 --> 00:16:52.778
and children will like it,

00:16:52.778 --> 00:16:54.612
and I only note that
because when I was a kid,

00:16:54.612 --> 00:16:56.748
there was no movies
that were for kids.

00:16:56.748 --> 00:16:58.683
There'd be like one a year.
-Yeah.

00:16:58.683 --> 00:17:01.186
-They do like "The Little
Mermaid" once a year.

00:17:01.186 --> 00:17:03.955
And the rest of the time it was
like parents would be like,

00:17:03.955 --> 00:17:05.090
"You're going to the movies."

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:06.558
You'd be like,
"What are we seeing?

00:17:06.558 --> 00:17:08.193
They'll be like, "Working Girl."

00:17:08.193 --> 00:17:09.427
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:17:09.427 --> 00:17:11.530
-"Just cover your eyes
the whole time."

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:12.831
[ Laughter ]

00:17:12.831 --> 00:17:15.366
-Your parents would take you to,
like, those adult dramas?

00:17:15.366 --> 00:17:16.868
-Yeah, yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:17:16.868 --> 00:17:18.803
-Really?
-No, for real, they did.

00:17:18.803 --> 00:17:21.573
I remember my mom
and her sisters took me,

00:17:21.573 --> 00:17:23.575
when I was maybe 7 or something,

00:17:23.575 --> 00:17:25.344
to see this movie
"Regarding Henry."

00:17:25.344 --> 00:17:26.744
Remember that?
-Sure. Yeah.

00:17:26.744 --> 00:17:29.681
-Hear the murmurs.
-Oh, yeah. Harrison Ford.

00:17:29.681 --> 00:17:30.882
-Harrison Ford, Annette Bening,

00:17:30.882 --> 00:17:33.918
and he's shot in the head,
and he has amnesia

00:17:33.918 --> 00:17:36.354
